[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814248257","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105282#issuecomment-2814248257","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105282","id":2814248257,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nvgVB","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T00:23:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T00:23:10Z","body":"We recently fixed physics interpolation with the `XRCamera3D` so it properly combines the latest tracking data with the interpolated data of the underlying physics object.\n\nAs there is no tracking here, that means we're getting a zero position and orientation for the camera at this point.\n\nIt is ALWAYS expected that the `XRCamera3D` node is positioned by the system and that any position you give it is overruled. That it \"works\" for you is more a fluke than expected behavior.\n\nThe recommendation is to have a separate rig for non-XR that uses a normal Camera node (seeing that also allows you to properly setup FOV and other p